, {"given": "Tao", "family": "Yu", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "29733", "event": {"name": "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37", "theme": "38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)", "location": "Vancouver, BC, Canada", "acronym": "NeurIPS 2024", "number": "37", "start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 10]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 15]]}}, "container-title": ["Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 19]], "date-time": "2026-06-19T15:44:39Z", "timestamp": 1781883879000}, "score": 50.801876, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.proceedings.com/079017-3421.html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.52202/079017-3421", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T14:14:37Z", "timestamp": 1785334477662, "version": "3.55.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 1]], "date-time": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1767225600000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://www.uspto.gov/ip-policy/copyright-policy/copyright-basics"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>This paper examines workflow transformation in agentic artificial intelligence for data science. The central question is: How do agentic systems change the division of labor across problem framing, data preparation, modeling, validation, and communication? We argue that the important shift is not that language models can write isolated snippets of code, but that agentic systems can bind intent clarification, tool use, iterative execution, error recovery, evidence synthesis, and stakeholder-facing explanation into one operational loop. This creates economic value by reducing coordination costs and expanding analytical capacity, yet it also changes the risk profile of data work: mistakes become more procedural, more compositional, and sometimes harder to detect. We develop a framework that treats the agent as an accountable analytical operator, evaluate implications for organizations, and propose design principles for robust deployment.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.6937638", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T13:53:47Z", "timestamp": 1785333227000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["From Copilot to Coworker: How LLM Agents Reshape End-to-End Data Science Workflows"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8977-2660", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Eledu", "family": "Shah", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T13:53:47Z", "timestamp": 1785333227000}, "score": 37.975918, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=6937638"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6937638", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 19]], "date-time": "2026-03-19T12:19:35Z", "timestamp": 1773922775181, "version": "3.50.1"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Instats Inc.", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>This workshop introduces Agentic Data Analytics, the next frontier in research automation. Unlike standard chatbots, autonomous AI agents can plan, execute, debug, and summarize an entire scientific analysis \u2014 and even draft the report. Using the free Google Antigravity tool, participants learn how to build reproducible agentic workflows using precise natural language, covering data cleaning, analysis, visualization, and report generation directly on their laptop.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.61700/85oqxe1omy90e2487", "type": "report", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 19]], "date-time": "2026-03-19T08:10:49Z", "timestamp": 1773907849000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Agentic Data Analytics: Automating Research Workflows"], "prefix": "10.61700", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1907-9700", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Peter", "family": "Gruber", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "47853", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 19]], "date-time": "2026-03-19T08:10:49Z", "timestamp": 1773907849000}, "score": 33.30002, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://instats.org/seminar/agentic-data-analytics-automating-resear"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.61700/85oqxe1omy90e2487", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 26]], "date-time": "2025-06-26T04:04:33Z", "timestamp": 1750910673252, "version": "3.41.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "ScienceTech Xplore", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["IJAIDSML"], "DOI": "10.63282/3050-9262.ijaidsml-v5i2p102", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 25]], "date-time": "2025-06-25T09:25:21Z", "timestamp": 1750843521000}, "page": "9-16", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Automating Data Engineering Workflows with AI and Machine Learning"], "prefix": "10.63282", "volume": "5", "author": [{"given": "Aditya", "family": "Banerjee", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "52640", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "container-title": ["International Journal of Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, and Machine Learning"], "original-title": ["English"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 25]], "date-time": "2025-06-25T09:25:23Z", "timestamp": 1750843523000}, "score": 32.82937, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://ijaidsml.org/index.php/ijaidsml/article/view/55"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.63282/3050-9262.ijaidsml-v5i2p102", "ISSN": ["3050-9262"], "issn-type": [{"value": "3050-9262", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2025-08-01T08:40:07Z", "timestamp": 1754037607479, "version": "3.41.2"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Madison Academic Press", "issue": "1", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["AETR"], "abstract": "<jats:p>This paper presents a comprehensive overview of the evolution of data science from a statistics-centric discipline to a machine learning\u2013driven field, culminating in the current integration of large language models (LLMs). It identifies key limitations in traditional LLM applications\u2014such as limited cross-domain adaptability, lack of interpretability, and workflow rigidity\u2014and explores recent innovations addressing these challenges. Three representative frameworks\u2014R&amp;D-Agent, SPIO, and Agent Laboratory\u2014illustrate LLMs\u2019 transition from assistive tools to autonomous agents capable of planning, executing, and optimizing entire data science workflows. These systems leverage dual-agent cooperation, modular architectures, and self-correcting capabilities to improve performance in end-to-end data analysis and scientific research. The paper concludes by outlining future priorities, including domain-specific customization, standardized agent evaluation, and improved interpretability, all of which are essential for the next generation of intelligent, autonomous data science systems.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.56028/aetr.14.1.1582.2025", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2025-08-01T07:55:12Z", "timestamp": 1754034912000}, "page": "1582", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["From Assistants to Agents: The Evolution of Large Language Models in Data Science Workflows"], "prefix": "10.56028", "volume": "14", "author": [{"given": "Xiyuan", "family": "Yin", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "35028", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 26]]}, "container-title": ["Advances in Engineering Technology Research"], "link": [{"URL": "https://admin.madison-publishing.com/index.php/aetr/article/download/3939/3961", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://admin.madison-publishing.com/index.php/aetr/article/download/3939/3961", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2025-08-01T08:04:20Z", "timestamp": 1754035460000}, "score": 31.146322, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://madison-proceedings.com/index.php/aetr/article/view/3939"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 26]]}, "references-count": 0, "journal-issue": {"issue": "1", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 27]]}}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.56028/aetr.14.1.1582.2025", "ISSN": ["2790-1688"], "issn-type": [{"value": "2790-1688", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 26]]}}], "items-per-page": 5, "query": {"start-index": 0, "search-terms": null}}}